🚽 Test case: a bare NATIVE call as the return expression of a void
🚽 function (`bussin yapping(...);`) must run the native exactly once and
🚽 not be reported as undefined. PR #254 skipped ast_accept()'s NODE_RETURN
🚽 pre-visit for bare calls (to stop `bussin make();` double-running); the
🚽 void/NONE arm compensates by executing the call itself, and must
🚽 dispatch native vs. user-defined the same way every other bare-call site
🚽 does (execute_function_call alone would search only the user table and
🚽 wrongly report `yapping` undefined -- PR #254 review, finding 1).
skibidi dump() {
    bussin yapping("inside dump");
}

skibidi main {
    dump();
    yapping("after dump");
}
